  "adapters": [
    "Shared Cell<u64> backing preserves live read/mutable aliases; slices use original bit offsets.",
    "Placement default construction retains the deliberately poisoned storage setup using MaybeUninit.",
    "Original 640 and 6400 iteration bounds, callback cancellation and assertion helper expansion are preserved.",
    "Uninitialised C++ backing words are safely initialised before otherwise identical writes; no asserted result depends on the old indeterminate bits.",
    "The zero-assertion SetEmpty smoke case is separately tracked and must complete, not disappear from execution."
